From: szabo@netcom.com (Nick Szabo)
Date: Fri, 2 Dec 1994 21:55:53 -0800 (PST)
Subject: [#94-12-97] BASICS: Anarchy

In our area, we have an entire university campus (Stanford) and 
surrounding suburbs (10,000+ people) where the roads, streets, etc. 
are all privately owned by the campus, which contracts out the police,
construction, maintenence, etc. work.  If I'm not mistaken, even the
huge upper-class mall next to the campus is owned by the University,
as is much of the adjacent industrial park (home to HP world headquarters,
Lockheed, Xerox PARC, biotech companies, etc.)  Not coincidentally, the 
univeristy lands also boast the largest the largest undeveloped natural 
areas on the middle and lower Penninsula between highway 280 and the Bay 
(unless perhaps you count the Bay flatland marshes).

Of course, there are innumerable malls, suburbs, etc. with privately
built operated streets in the U.S. and elswhere.  There are several 
private-sector superhighways even now being constructed in China, Mexico, 
and elsewhere.  The largest tunnel in the world, the Channel Tunnel was
privately built and is privately operated.  The notion that private road 
building is farfetched is itself absurd.

